# {{ title }}

## Links

- Inline: [YAMD on the web](https://yamd.example "The YAMD home page")
- Reference: [the CommonMark spec][commonmark], and [again][CommonMark] (labels ignore case)
- Collapsed reference: [CommonMark][]
- Angle brackets: <https://example.com/a(b)c>
- Email: <mailto:hello@yamd.example>

[commonmark]: https://spec.commonmark.org "CommonMark"

## Bare links

Bare URLs always become links: https://yamd.example/docs.
Trailing punctuation stays outside the link: see https://yamd.example/faq, or https://yamd.example/help!
Balanced parentheses stay inside: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markdown_(disambiguation)
To show a URL without linking it, use code: `https://not.a.link`.

## Links between documents

- Relative path: [the tables example](tables.yamd)
- A section in another file: [table captions](tables.yamd#captions)
- Wikilink: [[tables]]
- Wikilink to a section, with a label: [[tables#Captions|captions in tables]]
- Wikilink to another folder: [[../02-documents/directives]]
- A section in this document: [[#images]] or [the images section](#images)

## Images

Images take attributes for size and alignment:

![The YAMD team logo](../assets/team.svg){width=160}

![The YAMD team logo, centered](../assets/team.svg){width=200 align=center}

A reference-style image:

![The YAMD team logo, again][logo]

[logo]: ../assets/team.svg

### Figures

An image alone in its paragraph with a `caption` becomes a numbered figure:

![Requests go from the client through the gateway to storage](../assets/architecture.svg){caption="Request flow" #fig:flow width=480}

![The YAMD team](../assets/team.svg){caption="Our team" #fig:team width=240 align=center}

Refer to figures by label: [@fig:flow] shows the request path, and [@fig:team] shows the team.

### Decorative images

Images need alt text. Purely decorative ones say so explicitly:

![](../assets/divider.svg){decorative}
